{"t": 1794123726.2067091, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"path": "catalog/pager.py", "content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n"}, {"path": "tests/test_pager.py", "content": "import pytest\n\nfrom catalog.pager import page\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"items, number, size, expected\",\n    [\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 1, 2, [0, 1]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 2, 2, [2, 3]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 3, 2, [4]),\n        ([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 4, 2, []),\n        ([], 1, 2, []),\n        ([0, 1], 1, 1, [0]),\n    ],\n)\ndef test_page_uses_one_based_numbers(items, number, size, expected):\n    assert page(items, number, size) == expected\n"}], "message": "Fix one-based pagination offset for #57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794123730.132003, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\nFixes #57.\n\n- Calculate the slice offset as `(number - 1) * size` to honor the documented 1-based page numbers confirmed by #57.\n- Add regression coverage for the first and subsequent pages, a partial final page, out-of-range pages, empty input, and page size one.\n- Leave behavior for invalid page numbers and sizes unchanged; #57 specifies no new validation contract.\n\n## Verification\n`python -m pytest -q`\n- Before fix: 4 failed, 2 passed (reproduces the bug).\n- After fix: 6 passed.\n\nThe local workspace is not a Git checkout. Changes were published through the GitHub tools. Remote file-content reads returned empty results, so the implementation and tests were verified against the supplied local source.", "draft": false, "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination offset (#57)"}, "ok": true}
